"Both type and interface are used to define the structure of data in TypeScript. However, interfaces are mainly used to define object structures and support declaration merging. On the other hand, type aliases are more flexible because they support unions, intersections, primitive types, and tuples. I generally use interfaces for object structures and types for complex type combinations."
