"Union types allow a variable to have one of several possible types. We use the pipe symbol. For example, a variable can be either a string or a number.

Intersection types combine multiple types into one. We use the ampersand symbol. The resulting type must satisfy all the combined types.

I use union when a value can have different possible types, and intersection when I need to combine multiple object structures."

English Interview Answer
"Optional chaining allows us to safely access nested object properties without throwing an error when a property is null or undefined. We use the ?. operator.

Nullish coalescing provides a default value when the left-hand side is null or undefined. We use the ?? operator.

Optional chaining prevents errors during property access, while nullish coalescing helps us handle missing values."
